      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CAPTAINS KNOCK (10) is flying having landed the hat trick by leading and cruising home by 14m last week. Drops back to the mile but owns a good strike rate at it and while he draws a couple of spots deeper than last time he came from wider than this when scoring two back. RAKERO ROCKET NZ (11) hasn't raced since March but impressed in his first Australian campaign, highlighted by two big wins at this circuit and distance along with placings in the Newcastle Mile and a Miracle Mile qualifier. He'll be ready to go off two trials, easily winning the latest so could threaten. MAX DELIGHT (8) has ground to make up on CAPTAINS KNOCK through the last clash but he was held up there and is capable of better. BETTER ECLIPSE (9) could be best of the rest.",
